    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nDouble clicking does not take positition into consideration when mousemoveevent is on, resulting in clicking in two different places within `mousetime` count as double click.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim --clean`\n2. `:set mousemoveevent`\n3. Write some text\n4. Click one one location and then within `mousetime` click a different location\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nMulti-click detection should require the clicks to be at the same position.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.12.3\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNot applicable\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWindows Terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\n.\n\n### Installation\n\nWinget",
